---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About the Festival | PSFF Season 03">
  <div
    class="relative w-full bg-[#B31D12] text-[#FDFCF7] border-b-2 border-black py-16 sm:py-24 px-6 sm:px-12 selection:bg-[#FDB813] selection:text-[#B31D12] overflow-hidden"
  >
    <!-- Background Graph Grid, Swirls & Film Perforations -->
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none opacity-15 overflow-hidden"
    >
      <!-- Top & Bottom Film Reel Border Patterns -->
      <div
        class="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-4 border-b border-[#FDB813]/40"
        style="background-image: radial-gradient(#FDB813 35%, transparent 35%); background-size: 16px 16px;"
      >
      </div>
      <div
        class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 h-4 border-t border-[#FDB813]/40"
        style="background-image: radial-gradient(#FDB813 35%, transparent 35%); background-size: 16px 16px;"
      >
      </div>

      <!-- Golden Graph Grid Overlay -->
      <div
        class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10"
        style="background-image: linear-gradient(to right, #FDB813 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(to bottom, #FDB813 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 24px 24px;"
      >
      </div>

      <!-- Golden Traditional Swirl Vectors -->
      <svg
        class="absolute -left-24 top-1/4 w-[520px] h-[520px] text-[#FDB813]"
        viewBox="0 0 400 400"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
      >
        <path
          d="M50 200 C80 120, 160 80, 240 120 C320 160, 360 260, 290 330 C220 400, 100 370, 70 290 C40 210, 110 140, 190 140 C270 140, 310 220, 280 270 C250 320, 190 320, 160 280 C130 240, 150 190, 200 190"
        ></path>
        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="140" stroke-dasharray="8 8"></circle>
      </svg>
      <svg
        class="absolute -right-28 bottom-1/4 w-[520px] h-[520px] text-[#FDB813]"
        viewBox="0 0 400 400"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.5"
      >
        <path
          d="M50 200 C80 120, 160 80, 240 120 C320 160, 360 260, 290 330 C220 400, 100 370, 70 290 C40 210, 110 140, 190 140 C270 140, 310 220, 280 270 C250 320, 190 320, 160 280 C130 240, 150 190, 200 190"
        ></path>
        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="170" stroke-dasharray="6 6"></circle>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-16">
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <header class="border-b border-[#FDB813]/30 pb-8 space-y-3">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-200">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#FDB813] transition-colors"
            >&larr; Home</a
          > / About
        </div>
        <h1
          class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-white font-mono drop-shadow-sm"
        >
          About The Festival
        </h1>
        <p class="font-mono text-sm sm:text-base text-[#FDB813] font-bold">
          Pazhassi Short Film Festival (PSFF) &bull; Mananthavady, Wayanad
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Section 1: Genesis, Cultural Context & Civic Partnership -->
      <section
        class="space-y-6 text-zinc-100 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed"
      >
        <div class="border-b border-[#FDB813]/30 pb-2">
          <h2
            class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-white font-mono"
          >
            The Genesis &amp; Cultural Roots
          </h2>
        </div>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          The Pazhassi Short Film Festival was conceived to address a
          long-standing void in the cultural landscape of Wayanad: the lack of
          an authentic theatrical platform dedicated entirely to independent
          short-form cinema. While short films, documentaries, and experimental
          projects frequently flourish online or in major urban circuits,
          grassroots audiences and aspiring regional filmmakers rarely share a
          physical cinema space to experience and debate these works together.
        </p>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          Timed to coincide with the annual Pazhassi Day observance, the
          festival draws inspiration from the enduring legacy of resistance and
          self-determination associated with Pazhassi Raja. The event is curated
          and executed as a collaborative cultural initiative by <strong
            class="text-[#FDB813]">Drishtidosham Chalachithravedi</strong
          >, a dedicated film society collective; the historic <strong
            class="text-[#FDB813]">Pazhassi Raja Smaraka Granthalayam</strong
          >, which serves as a center for literary and intellectual life in
          Mananthavady; and the <strong class="text-[#FDB813]"
            >Mananthavady Municipality</strong
          >, providing civic patronage and community infrastructure.
        </p>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          Admission to every screening, panel discussion, and open forum is kept
          entirely free of charge. This deliberate non-commercial stance ensures
          that students, local cinema enthusiasts, visiting delegates, and
          seasoned film practitioners gather on equal footing inside a
          commercial movie house.
        </p>

        <!-- Inline Highlight Frame: The Screening Venue -->
        <div
          class="border border-[#FDB813]/40 bg-[#8B140B]/90 p-4 sm:p-6 rounded-xl shadow-[4px_4px_0px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)] space-y-3 mt-6 backdrop-blur-xs"
        >
          <div
            class="border border-[#FDB813]/30 h-[340px] sm:h-[440px] bg-[#5C0D07] rounded-lg p-2 flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden shadow-inner"
          >
            <img
              src="https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/gps-cs-s/AHRPTWk2MknLWIqh0cH_T_5SS4ZCOdQ6m98hAcivf5327pxGbv8fUboHDcGpPJvXS2pp5KtSpx5SOrcdXIMm9CvRB5LnRjq8bGdIyN9oG_bDxkXMZbA1L8D_nNsTYjbPlSHgPnRHS_8=s1360-w1360-h1020-rw"
              alt="Veena - Varna Theatre complex in Mananthavady"
              class="w-full h-full object-contain"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <p
            class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#FDB813] text-center"
          >
            Veena - Varna Theatre, Mananthavady &mdash; The Festival Home &amp;
            Screening Complex
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Festival Architecture & Curation Model -->
      <section
        class="space-y-6 text-zinc-100 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed border-t border-[#FDB813]/30 pt-10"
      >
        <div class="border-b border-[#FDB813]/30 pb-2">
          <h2
            class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-white font-mono"
          >
            Two-Tier Curation &amp; Adjudication Framework
          </h2>
        </div>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          PSFF follows a rigorous two-tier selection and judging model designed
          to maintain absolute transparency and artistic integrity. In the
          preliminary phase, every valid submission is reviewed by a 12-member
          internal screening panel comprising film society organizers, writers,
          and cultural practitioners. This committee pares down all received
          entries to a strictly curated competition shortlist of exactly 10
          short films.
        </p>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          During the festival day, these 10 official selections are projected on
          the big screen at Veena - Varna Theatre. An independent main jury
          consisting of renowned film industry directors and critics evaluates
          the films on calibrated parameters including screenplay structure,
          directorial control, cinematography, sound design, and thematic
          coherence. Parallel to the jury's scoring, the audience votes directly
          at the venue to decide the Popular Film award.
        </p>

        <!-- Inline Highlight Frame: Filmmakers & Public Debates -->
        <div
          class="border border-[#FDB813]/40 bg-[#8B140B]/90 p-4 sm:p-6 rounded-xl shadow-[4px_4px_0px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)] space-y-3 mt-6 backdrop-blur-xs"
        >
          <div
            class="border border-[#FDB813]/30 h-[340px] sm:h-[440px] bg-[#5C0D07] rounded-lg p-2 flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden shadow-inner"
          >
            <img
              src="https://i.ibb.co/mC4H1MgK/1.jpg"
              alt="Open forum interaction between filmmakers and festival delegates"
              class="w-full h-full object-contain"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <p
            class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#FDB813] text-center"
          >
            Open Forum &amp; Direct Dialogue Between Filmmakers, Jury Members,
            and Delegates
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: The Journey — Seasons 01 & 02 -->
      <section
        class="space-y-6 text-zinc-100 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed border-t border-[#FDB813]/30 pt-10"
      >
        <div class="border-b border-[#FDB813]/30 pb-2">
          <h2
            class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-white font-mono"
          >
            The Journey &amp; Past Milestones
          </h2>
        </div>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          The inaugural edition took place on <strong class="text-[#FDB813]"
            >30 November 2024</strong
          > under the jury leadership of Sanath PC. The debut season immediately captured
          the attention of independent filmmakers statewide, culminating in Waseem
          Ameer's <em>The Show</em> winning the inaugural Best Short Film title, Nandulal
          M receiving Best Director for <em>Kolam</em>, and Atul Raj's <em
            >Chudalamadan</em
          > securing the audience-voted Best Popular Film accolade.
        </p>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          Season 02, staged on <strong class="text-[#FDB813]"
            >29 November 2025</strong
          >, represented a massive leap in scale and community participation.
          The edition was officially inaugurated by Kerala State Film
          Award-winning art director Ajayan Chalissery (<em>Manjummel Boys</em
          >), with an evaluation jury chaired by acclaimed screenwriter and
          director Santhosh Mandoor. Out of 55 statewide submissions, the top 10
          films were presented inside the auditorium and simultaneously
          broadcast outdoors via an expansive LED wall setup to accommodate
          overflow crowds.
        </p>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          The second season also marked two major technical milestones: the
          introduction of a custom electronic voting system for the ₹10,000
          Popular Film award and the addition of the Best Cinematographer
          category. Mridul S's nuanced short film <em>Kanam</em> swept both the Best
          Short Film award (₹25,000) and the Popular Film award, while Sruthil Mathew
          took Best Director (₹15,000) for <em>Ura</em>, and Nijo Abraham earned
          the inaugural Best Cinematographer laurel (₹10,000) for <em
            >Golden Love</em
          >.
        </p>

        <!-- Two-Column Photo Pair: Audience & Award Moments from Season 02 -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mt-6">
          <div
            class="border border-[#FDB813]/40 bg-[#8B140B]/90 p-4 rounded-xl shadow-[4px_4px_0px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)] space-y-2 backdrop-blur-xs"
          >
            <div
              class="border border-[#FDB813]/30 h-[280px] sm:h-[320px] bg-[#5C0D07] rounded-lg p-1.5 flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden shadow-inner"
            >
              <img
                src="https://i.ibb.co/JwZj6Tdk/4.jpg"
                alt="Packed auditorium at Veena - Varna Theatre during Season 02 screenings"
                class="w-full h-full object-contain"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
            <p
              class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#FDB813] text-center"
            >
              Packed Auditorium at Season 02 Public Screenings
            </p>
          </div>

          <div
            class="border border-[#FDB813]/40 bg-[#8B140B]/90 p-4 rounded-xl shadow-[4px_4px_0px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)] space-y-2 backdrop-blur-xs"
          >
            <div
              class="border border-[#FDB813]/30 h-[280px] sm:h-[320px] bg-[#5C0D07] rounded-lg p-1.5 flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden shadow-inner"
            >
              <img
                src="https://i.ibb.co/YTKSmkLj/Best-Film.jpg"
                alt="Season 02 Best Film presentation ceremony for Kanam"
                class="w-full h-full object-contain"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
            <p
              class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#FDB813] text-center"
            >
              Best Short Film Award Presentation &mdash; Kanam (Season 02)
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Looking Forward to Season 03 -->
      <section
        class="space-y-6 text-zinc-100 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed border-t border-[#FDB813]/30 pt-10"
      >
        <div class="border-b border-[#FDB813]/30 pb-2">
          <h2
            class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-white font-mono"
          >
            Season 03 (2026) Directorate &amp; Vision
          </h2>
        </div>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          Scheduled for <strong class="text-[#FDB813]">28 November 2026</strong
          >, PSFF Season 03 expands its commitment to independent cinema.
          National Film Award–winning filmmaker Sherry Govindan serves as the
          Chief Jury, working alongside film critic and director Arjun K to
          assess competitive entries.
        </p>

        <p class="font-sans leading-relaxed text-zinc-100">
          The total festival endowment has been established at ₹62,500, honoring
          winners across Best Short Film (₹25,000), Best Director (₹15,000),
          Best Cinematographer (₹10,000), and Best Popular Film (₹10,000), along
          with ₹2,500 cash consolation grants awarded to each remaining
          non-winning film within the curated Top 10 Official Selection.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Bottom Submission Route -->
      <div
        class="border-2 border-black bg-[#8B140B] text-[#FDFCF7] p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-2xl shadow-[6px_6px_0px_0px_#000000] flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-6"
      >
        <div class="space-y-1.5">
          <h3
            class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-white font-mono"
          >
            Enter Your Work for Season 03
          </h3>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-200">
            Submissions open until 30 September 2026 &bull; Runtime not
            exceeding 30 minutes
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/submit"
            class="inline-block px-7 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-[#B31D12] bg-[#FDB813] hover:bg-white border-2 border-black rounded-lg transition-all shadow-[3px_3px_0px_0px_#000000] hover:-translate-y-0.5 cursor-pointer"
          >
            Submit Film &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
